-- statement:
--   For any finite family of genuine bounded right-continuous-filtration stopping times on the canonical arbitrary-jump X, the same-space Gaussian component Y and the original discounted ruin-gated C2 reserve gradient/Hessian have an integrable sum of bilinear weighted increments. The exact expectation is the sum of h_i sigma_X squared times the corresponding source gradient-Hessian expectations. All coefficient predictability and moments are automatic under explicit uniform bounds.
